## Stop Lakebase control-plane routes from freezing the server

Context: On a workspace without Lakebase, opening Settings triggered
GET /settings/graph-engine/lakebase-projects. The async route called the
synchronous Databricks Postgres API directly on the event loop; the API hung
until the SDK's 5-minute retry timeout, so every other request (including
/health) stalled and the UI became unreachable.

Changes:

1. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   Wrap all 11 /graph-engine/lakebase-* handlers (health, projects, branches,
   pg-databases, pg-schemas, objects, sync-objects, drop-object, pg-roles,
   grant-superuser, provision) in `await run_blocking(...)` so slow
   control-plane calls run in the thread pool instead of blocking the loop
   (.coding_rules §5 async discipline).
2. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   `graph_engine_lakebase_projects_result` returns an empty project list with
   an explanatory message in local Postgres mode (PGPASSWORD set) without
   calling the Postgres API.
3. tests/units/settings/test_lakebase_projects.py
   Clear PGPASSWORD in the pagination test; add a test asserting local
   Postgres mode never builds a WorkspaceClient.

Modified files:
- src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
- src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
- tests/units/settings/test_lakebase_projects.py

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 5856 passed, 315 skipped,
6 deselected, 32 warnings in 24.07s
Manual: /settings/graph-engine/lakebase-projects → 200 in 0.008s; while a slow
lakebase-branches call was in flight, GET / answered in 0.30s.

## Make ontology generation work on databricks-claude-opus-5

### Context
Running the ontology wizard against `databricks-claude-opus-5` failed on
every iteration: the endpoint enables extended thinking by default, so
reasoning blocks consumed the whole `max_tokens` budget and completions ended
with `finish_reason=length` and 0 text characters. Once thinking was off, a
10-table schema (one table with 227 columns) still overflowed the hard-coded
8192-token output budget, even though this endpoint accepts 32000.

### Changes
1. `src/agents/engine_base.py` — send `thinking: {"type": "disabled"}` to
   Claude endpoints; if an endpoint rejects it ("Extra inputs are not
   permitted"), strip it, cache the ban per endpoint and retry once (same
   mechanism already used for `temperature`).
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/engine.py` — output-token budget is now
   configurable via `ONTOBRICKS_OWL_MAX_TOKENS` (default 8192); the per-call
   timeout scales proportionally.
3. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_engine_base.py` — tests for thinking on
   Claude endpoints, omission on other endpoints, and drop-and-retry on 400.
4. `.env.example` — documents `ONTOBRICKS_OWL_MAX_TOKENS`.

### Modified files
- src/agents/engine_base.py
- src/agents/agent_owl_generator/engine.py
- tests/units/agents/test_agent_engine_base.py
- .env.example

### Test result
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` — 5859 passed, 315 skipped.

## Stop prose-prefixed ontology answers from skipping quality gates

### Context
`databricks-claude-opus-5` answered "No documents available; schemas are
complete." followed by the Turtle. The `@prefix` gate in the OWL generator
loop then skipped the class-cap guard, the pitfall fix loop and the Stage-1
evaluator, while the final-accept branch still took the text — so the
ontology was saved unchecked (`iteration_summary=[]`, `generation_score=null`).

### Changes
1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/engine.py` — new `_strip_turtle_preamble`
   removes leading prose / an opening code fence (and the matching trailing
   fence) before `@prefix`; applied to every text answer so the gates run on
   the Turtle itself. Answers without a preamble are left byte-identical.
2. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_owl_generator_preamble.py` — unit tests for
   prose, code fences, clean Turtle, prose-only and inline `@prefix` mentions.

### Modified files
- src/agents/agent_owl_generator/engine.py
- tests/units/agents/test_agent_owl_generator_preamble.py (new)

### Test result
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` — 5875 passed, 304 skipped
(the `pitfalls` extra is now installed locally, un-skipping 11 tests).

## Auto-map: stop silently dropping truncated tool calls

### Context
Auto-Map on a 12-class ontology logged
"tool_submit_entity_mapping: missing required fields" repeatedly. The agent
called the LLM with `max_tokens=2048`; a wide entity (31 attributes, full
SELECT + attribute map) overflowed it, the tool-call JSON was cut off, the
engine replaced the undecodable arguments with `{}`, and the model only saw
"class_uri and sql_query are required" — so it resent the same oversized call.

### Changes
1. `src/agents/agent_auto_assignment/engine.py` — output budget raised to
   `_MAX_TOKENS = 8192`; tool calls whose arguments are not valid JSON are no
   longer dispatched with `{}`: the model gets an explicit "arguments were cut
   off" tool error and a WARNING is logged with `finish_reason`.
2. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_auto_assignment_truncated_args.py` — new
   tests: truncated arguments are not dispatched, the model is told the call
   was cut off, and the budget fits wide entity payloads.

### Modified files
- src/agents/agent_auto_assignment/engine.py
- tests/units/agents/test_agent_auto_assignment_truncated_args.py (new)

### Test result
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` — 5878 passed, 304 skipped.
